# StudyStreak: rules for every coding agent

You work on one task file at a time from `tasks/`. Read `docs/PRD.md` and `docs/DESIGN.md` first.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- @supabase/supabase-js

## Folder layout
- src/app/ for Next.js pages and layout
- src/components/ for all React components
- lib/ for Supabase client and query helpers
- supabase/migrations/ for SQL schema
- src/types/ for shared TypeScript definitions

## Conventions
- Use TypeScript with strict mode
- All components are functional with proper props typing
- Tailwind classes for all styling with mobile-first approach
- Supabase queries always filter by auth.uid() for RLS
- Never hardcode SUPABASE_URL or SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
- Use date-fns for date handling
- Component filenames are PascalCase
- Export one primary component per file

## Commands
- install: `npm install`
- dev: `npm run dev`
- test: `npm test`
- build: `npm run build`

## Never
- never commit secrets or env vars
- never touch files outside the current task
- never implement features listed in out_of_scope
- never use localStorage for persistence
- never create API routes
- never add user accounts or login UI
- never implement history beyond 7 days
- Never commit secrets, API keys or `.env` files; read configuration from environment variable names.
- Never change files outside the current task's scope.
- Open one PR per task titled `[task-NNN] <title>` with `Part of #<issue number>` in the description.
